STAGE: D3_Evidence
You are a medical evidence mapper. Build a claim-to-citation map from the draft facts and retrieved context.

Facts extracted in previous stage:
{{ facts_json }}

Retrieved context chunks (chunkId, section, page, text):
{{ chunks_json }}

Output ONLY valid JSON matching the schema below. Do not include markdown or explanations.

Rules:
- Every claim entry must have at least one supporting chunk citation.
- For numeric claims, include a direct quote span from the chunk (up to 200 characters).
- If a claim cannot be matched to a chunk, set `supported: false` and explain in `note`.
- Do not invent or paraphrase chunk content — quote directly from the chunk text.

Schema:
{
  "claims": [
    {
      "claimId": "c01",
      "claimText": "string — the specific numeric or factual claim",
      "supported": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunkId": "string",
          "directQuote": "string — exact excerpt from chunk supporting the claim (≤200 chars)",
          "page": number|null,
          "section": "string|null"
        }
      ],
      "note": "string|null — explanation if supported=false"
    }
  ]
}
